@node Intro "MS-Comment v1.3 Introductions"

For shure you remember the Multi Sysop Comment v1.2 released few Weeks
ago. Well, the Version 1.2 was good as nothing else, but look what bet
the update, this is for shure the best Multi Commenter available right
now. This Version features the following Options:

1. Unlimited Sysops & CoSysop
2. Set up an default Sysop by pressing Return only
3. Forwarding Mail to another Sys(CoSys)op
4. Seperate Output for Sysops and CoSysops
5. Supporting Prompt Line
6. Better @{" Design "Link Examp}
7. Complete Setup about an Icon
8. Possible to make it resident
9. Smaller and faster Code
But install it and enjoy the Power of this Door.

NOTE: The MS-Comment v1.3 is 100% BackDoor Free, if you dont believe them
      call @{" Marleys Coffee Shop "Link Marleys} for your private Version.

                             @{" Main Menu "Link MAIN} @{" Exit "QUIT}

@endnode

@node Requi "Requirements to run MS-Comment 1.3"

All what you need is the following:

1. Kickstart 2.0 or higher
2. A full installed Version of AmiExpress vX.xx
3. A assigned Directory called Doors:

and nothing else...                  @{" Main Menu "Link MAIN} @{" Exit "QUIT}

@endnode

@node Insta "Installation of MS-Comment v1.3"

After unpacking the TRSI-C13.LHA copy the whole Directory Comment from the
Archive to your DOORS:
Copy the BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/C.Info to your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/
After copying the Files jump into the Doors:Comment/ Directory and open the
Comment.Info for configuration the MS-Comment.
The following @{" ToolTypes "Link Toolt} are available.
If you have setup the Comment.Info the Installation is done, and you can join
your new Comment Door.

@endnode

@node Toolt "All ToolType Informations"

NAME.<#>=<Sysop Name>
---------------------
Eg:
NAME.1=Dr.Dre!/TRSI
NAME.2=J.Walker/TRSI
NAME.3=McLoud/TRSI
and so on set up how much Sysops you want.
------------------------------------------

DESC.<#>=<Sysop Funktion>
-------------------------
This is the funktion from the Sysop(s). DESC.1 means thats this is the
Funktion from Sysop #1 and so on....
Eg:
DESC.1=The big Boss is watching you
DESC.2=Console Cosysop & Nuker
DESC.3=TRSI World Leader
------------------------------------------

ANSWER.<#>=<Some Bullshit as Answer by choosen them>
----------------------------------------------------
This are the Answer Lines which are displayed by choosen the different
Sysop(s). ANSWER.1 is the Answer Line from Sysop #1, and so on.
Eg:
ANSWER.1=Remember the other Sysops
ANSWER.2=Thanx for leavin Mail
ANSWER.3=Why me ??? 
----------------------------------------------------

DEFAULT_SYSOP=<#>=<Number from the Sysop which should be the default Sysop>
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Here you can setup a default Sysop, this Sysop will be choosen by pressing
Return only.
Eg:
DEFAULT_SYSOP=1
means default Sysop is Sysop #1
----------------------------------------------------

FORWARD_FROM=<#>=<Number from the Sysop which should be forwarding Mail>
FORWARD_TO=<#>=<Number from the Sysop to send the forwarding Mails>
------------------------------------------------------------------------
This ToolTypes are only together sensefull.
May you are the Sysop and you go to Holiday and wish thats are all your
Mails forward to another Sysop then setup this ToolTypes.
Eg:
FORWARD_FROM=1
FORWARD_TO=3
This means if a User choose Sysop 1 the Mail will go automatically to
Sysop 3.
another example:
FORWARD_FROM=5
FORWARD_TO=1
This means if a User choose Sysop 5 the Mail will go automatically to
Sysop 1.
I hope this explains this usefull Option.
----------------------------------------------------

COSYSOP_FROM=<#>=<Number where starts the Cosysop to insert a seperate Line>
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Here you can specify from where on the CoSysops starts, to add a Line bet-
ween the Sysops and CoSysop(s)
Eg:
COSYSOP_FROM=4
This means Sysop 1-3 are Sysops, and all Sysops higher as 3 are Cosysops.
MS-Comment adds now a line between the Sysops & Cosysops.
Like this @{" Example "Link Examp}.
----------------------------------------------------

I hope everybody understand all the ToolTypes, it is a bit hard to explain
them coz my English is really sick...

                             @{" Main Menu "Link MAIN} @{" Exit "QUIT}

@endnode

@node news "What is new in MS-Comment 1.3"



                       UPDATE from MCS v1.2 to v1.3
                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

1. Supporting AmiExpress PromptLine.
   If you press c 3 at the Prompt, you will not jump to the Sysop
   Menu, now you jump directly to the msgbase. If the Sysop does not
   exists you will jump into the Sysop Menu.
2. Adding 2 new ToolTypes on XTC!`s Suggestion, called FORWARD_FROM=<#>
   and FORWARD_TO=<#>, if you set this ToolTypes, then it is possible to
   forward Mails from one Sysop to another Sysop.
3. Faster and shorter Code.
4. Adding new ToolType on AMICOM/MST`s Suggestion, called COSYSOP_FROM=<#>
   If you set them the MSC will add a seperate Line between the Sysops
   and CoSysops.
5. New Design

                             @{" Main Menu "Link MAIN} @{" Exit "QUIT}

@endnode

